 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to a license\nto sell liquor at retail for consumption on certain premises",
    "basePrintNo": "S7943",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7943-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §64, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7943\n\nSPONSOR: LITTLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to a\nlicense to sell liquor at retail for consumption on certain premises\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill will authorize the issuing of a retail liquor license to a\nbusiness in the County of Washington that is within a two hundred foot\nproximity of a religious institution.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Subdivision 7 of section 64 of the alcoholic beverage 2\ncontrol law is amended by adding a new paragraph (e-10) to authorize the\nissuing of a retail license for on-premises consumption for a premises\nwhich shall be located within two hundred feet of a building occupied as\na church, synagogue or other place of worship, provided such premises\nconstitute a premises for the sale of food or beverages at retail for\nconsumption on the premises located wholly within the boundaries of the\ncounty of Washington.\n\nSection 2: Provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMany small urban communities across the State are facing an uphill\nbattle when it comes to developing and restoring their historic down-\ntowns. Many of these historic villages and cities have existing downtown\ninfrastructures that situate places of worship in the same proximity as\nvarious store fronts and restaurants. This bill will allow for a down-\ntown restaurant in the Village of Hudson Falls to obtain a retail liquor\nlicense. By allowing this restaurant a liquor license they will be able\nto open their door to more patrons and help draw more people to downtown\nHudson Falls.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
